bgfx maps TextureFormat::BC1 to VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGB_UNORM_BLOCK, the alpha-less
BC1 variant that decodes the c0<=c1 punch-through mode as opaque black. Every
other bgfx backend gives BC1 punch-through-alpha semantics (D3D11
DXGI_FORMAT_BC1_UNORM, Metal MTLPixelFormatBC1_RGBA, and bimg's own CPU
decoder decodeBlockDxt1 writes {0,0,0,0}), as did the D3D9 D3DFMT_DXT1 the
WoW 3.3.5a client shipped against. On drivers with native BC support (RADV)
the RGB variant made every DXT1-with-1-bit-alpha texture (foliage, UI cutout
art, chat tabs) render opaque black; MoltenVK masked it because Apple GPUs
report BC1 unsupported and bgfx falls back to the alpha-correct CPU decode.
BC1_RGB and BC1_RGBA are jointly gated by textureCompressionBC, so support is
identical.
--- a/bgfx/src/renderer_vk.cpp
+++ b/bgfx/src/renderer_vk.cpp
@@ -167,5 +167,5 @@
 #define $G VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_G
 #define $B VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_B
 #define $A VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_A
-		{ VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGB_UNORM_BLOCK,       VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGB_UNORM_BLOCK,      VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED,           VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGB_SRGB_BLOCK,       { $_, $_, $_, $_ } }, // BC1
+		{ VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGBA_UNORM_BLOCK,      VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGBA_UNORM_BLOCK,     VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED,           VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGBA_SRGB_BLOCK,      { $_, $_, $_, $_ } }, // BC1
         { VK_FORMAT_BC2_UNORM_BLOCK,           VK_FORMAT_BC2_UNORM_BLOCK,          VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED,           VK_FORMAT_BC2_SRGB_BLOCK,           { $_, $_, $_, $_ } }, // BC2
